1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Now, the selected UV case can be automatically filled to the designated position.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Go to the UV editor window to check and click on the new UV filling tool.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
In the dialogue window, the filling direction is set to the interval between the UV cases.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
The filling ratio is set to the percentage of the area occupied by the UV case.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Calculate based on the UV map you have chosen.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,000
High-select rotation will allow the UV case to rotate according to the settings.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Fix the resolution ratio.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Fix the ratio of the UV cases selected at the time of selection.

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Click on the application to check the effect after filling.

10
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,000
You can also fill the UV case to other UV frames.

11
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Select all UV cases of the COS version.

12
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Change to the selected frame option.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Click on the application to fill.

14
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Insert or export multiple virtual models in the FBX format at the same time.

15
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
It will help you better complete multi-character scene production without limiting to single character.

16
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000
When you need to add additional virtual models to the scene, please confirm the download type as an addition.

17
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Under the move option, I will set the vertical axis to move 2 meters,

18
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,000
so that two models can be controlled.

19
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Open the animation editor window to check the virtual model animation.

20
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,000
When you add a costume to the scene,

21
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,000
you can also set the movement value for it to match the virtual model.

22
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Open the simulation and record the animation to check the final result.

23
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Through the FBX, you can choose to export all virtual models.

24
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
You can also export all virtual models or some specific virtual models.

25
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Through the roll-up function, you can roll up the opening position of the costume in a simpler way,

26
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,000
such as the sleeve, the pants, and so on.

27
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Use the edit version tool to select the outline of the 2D version.

28
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Here, select the sleeve line.

29
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Click on the right button to select the roll-up in the pop-up menu.

30
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:46,000
You can set the number of rolls up to three times.

31
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
You can also choose the length of each roll-up.

32
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,000
At least 10 mm, at most 200 mm.

33
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,000
To make it easier for you to check the position after rolling up,

34
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,000
the costume in the 3D window will appear.

35
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Click on the application to apply the input value and roll up the costume.

36
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Open the simulation to get the natural simulation effect.

37
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,000
At present, the roll-up function does not support symmetrical or continuous modification.

38
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
However, when you use this function again,

39
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
it will automatically use the data from the previous time.

40
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,000
If you need to make an asymmetrical effect,

41
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,000
you can also manually modify the value.

42
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,000
After clicking on the application, the roll-up window is still running.

43
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,000
You can choose whether to reset the roll-up position according to your needs,

44
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,000
and return it to the original shape of the costume.

45
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
After resetting, you can set the value according to your needs and apply the roll-up again.

46
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Selecting the roll-up function will make you choose the roll-up

47
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
with all the roll-ups with the selected roll-up.

48
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,000
In this example, we have deleted the roll-up between the left sleeve part and the body.

49
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
When we select a roll-up in the 2D or 3D window,

50
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,000
go to the main menu and edit the roll-up with all the roll-ups.

51
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,000
At this time, all the roll-ups with the roll-up directly or indirectly with this roll-up

52
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
will be selected together.

53
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Then you can move them together.

54
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,000
When you use the adjustment roll-up tool in the 2D window

55
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:52,000
or in the 3D window,

56
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
you can use the move tool to double-click a roll-up,

57
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,000
and you can also select all the roll-ups with the selected roll-up.

58
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:02,000
When you press the Shift key to do the multiple selection,

59
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,000
if you double-click a roll-up,

60
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:07,000
you will also select all the roll-ups with the selected roll-up.

61
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Please note that the items of the chain, side, button, inner shape, and roll-up roll-up

62
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
cannot be selected through the option of selecting all the roll-ups with the selected roll-up.

63
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
However, by connecting the roll-up to the roll-up with the pull-up function,

64
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:20,000
you can select them all through this function.

65
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,000
The USD file is now supported by a unified UV coordinate.

66
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
Now when you export the USD file,

67
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:30,000
you can find and select a unified UV coordinate in the pop-up window.

68
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,000
After selecting this option,

69
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,000
you can set the pixels of the UV sticker.

70
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Select the fill-in-primitive border,

71
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
you can extend it along the primitive border.

72
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:43,000
After completion, select Confirm.

73
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:46,000
This option is also applicable to NVIDIA Omniverse Connector,

74
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
and can be imported to Adobe Photoshop

75
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
via the Omniverse Connector Live Link.

76
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
This option is more stable than SubstancePaint.

